{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Id":118940,"Title":"mentioned you in this post","Message":"Hello!\n\nThis message is to notify you that snswedding2016 mentioned you in a post.\n\nThe post that you were mentioned in can be found here:\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79615-azul-fives-by-karisma-brides-2016\/?view=findpost&p=1905341\n\n----------------------------------\n@\"hirvine83\" I'm getting married at Azul Fives in January 2016. Most of my planning is done, just trying to tackle the to do list for the home stretch. I'm going to the BDR this Sunday!! I'm so excited to see the resort in person finally. Let me know if you have any specific questions and I can report back for you.  <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>\n \nHappy planning!\n----------------------------------\n\nIf you no longer wish to receive notifications of posts you are mentioned in, you can adjust your preferences on the\ncommunity by clicking My Settings, and then choosing Notification Options.\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/index.php\n\n","Sender":{"Id":281055,"Name":"snswedding2016","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281055.jpg?_r=1415590512","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":150,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1443098500,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":118356,"Title":"has replied to a personal conversation","Message":"hirvine83,\n\nTinkerSofi has replied to a personal conversation entitled \"Congratulations on your wedding!\".\n\nTinkerSofi said:\n======================================================================\nWe actually rented their sound system for $250 and I bought the wedding dj app and played music from my iphone. It worked perfectly, we had our own music and the sound system was definitely loud enough. It was just more work upfront I guess making the playlists but it all went really smoothly. I posted a review on a thread that someone opened, if you search wedding dj app you will probably find it. \n \nIt was windy at the sky deck, but it was sooo hot that the wind was actually really nice. The garden is nice, but definitely less private. If anyone is walking by at night they can see your wedding. We had 3 people come up from the zky bar up to the sky deck to see what was happening, but it was very private. As I said before, if you have the budget to do the whole thing up there, do it, you really won't regret it <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>. No one complained about the wind at all. \n \nThe entertainment was good I thought. It wasn't anything crazy, but they had a Mexican fiesta one day at the beach and that was nice. We missed most of it because we had reservations at the Thai restaurant, but we caught the last little bit of it. Then they have some live music and things like that. Had I gone as a couple maybe I would have found it a little boring and I would have ventured out to Playa a little more during the evenings, but if you're traveling as a group you really have nothing to worry about. We went to the zky bar after dinner every night and either danced the night away or had some drinks. Just being with such a large group made it fun, I didn't really even pay much attention to the hotel's entertainment. \n \nI put up some more pictures on my gallery on my profile. I'm waiting for the pictures from my photographer. I only have the raw images, but I want to get the edited ones before I post them <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>. He sent them on Sept 18 so I hope to get them soon! \n \n \n======================================================================\n\nPLEASE DO NOT REPLY DIRECTLY TO THIS EMAIL!\nYou can reply to this personal conversation by following the link below:\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/index.php?app=members&module=messaging&section=view&do=findMessage&topicID=11488&msgID=__firstUnread__\n","Sender":{"Id":265511,"Name":"TinkerSofi","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-265511.jpg?_r=1442890536","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1442875786,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Conversation","RelatedItemId":11488},{"Id":118128,"Title":"has replied to a personal conversation","Message":"hirvine83,\n\nTinkerSofi has replied to a personal conversation entitled \"Congratulations on your wedding!\".\n\nTinkerSofi said:\n======================================================================\nHi! Sorry for taking so long to reply. My hubby and I just moved so we're trying to get settled, which means not much time online haha. \n \nWe did the ceremony and cereption at the sky deck. We did pay the surcharge to have both of them up there, but it is so worth it. It is 100% private, and the view is just breathtaking up there. We had 30 guests plus us two, which made it a nice number in terms of paying for all those extra fees to have the sky deck haha. We had plenty of room to dance, stand and talk, etc. Whatever people wanted to do. My only regret is not being able to pay for extra time for our reception up there <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/sad.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':(' \/>. I don't regret it financially haha, but the time just went by so quickly. \n \nWe only picked a package for the reception tables, the vintage elegance package. So that was $250 for each table (we had 4 of them). For the ceremony we got the basic stuff, and then the day of the wedding they asked us if we wanted the chair covers only for the vintage elegance theme for $150 so I agreed. It was kind of expensive for just 30 chairs, but when I saw it, I thought it definitely added to the whole thing! I didn't have a lot of decor before so I think it would have looked a little empty had I not added those chairs. \n \nThe wedding itself costed us $6000 and a bit. This was only the payment we made to Karisma before we even arrived. Our photographer cost us $900 and so did our videographer. Then, while on site, I added the chair covers for the ceremony for $150, the set up fee was also something like $150 or 160. I also paid for the bridal suite at the spa which was about $200. My mom helped me pay for that, and while it was a little expensive, you get a whole day at the spa before your wedding, incl. your hair and makeup. Also, your bridal party can come and change with you. The services at the spa were amazing. I had the free hair and makeup for booking with a Karisma certified agent but I passed that on to my mom and I used the one included in the bridal package.\n \nI won't say that the wedding was a luxury, we didn't go overboard on decor, I didn't really have real flowers except for my bouquet, it was a  small group (as I said, 30), we didn't have a DJ. I have seen weddings where the brides go all out, so it is possible to do it at this resort if that's what you want. It will cost you an arm and leg, but know that there are also ways of making the wedding affordable.  In all honesty, I didn't miss any of the things we didn't have. At no point did I say, gee, I really wish we had a DJ, or those real flowers would have made a huge difference. I was happy with the choices we made. Guests were amazed anyway, just the setting on to itself is amazing, you don't need much to make it extraordinary <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/> \n \nI know that the prices have gone up a bit since we booked, we had the 2014 prices. So if you do decide to go with Karisma, don't wait too long to book. I know the prices go up a little every year. \n \nI hope this helps but let me know if you have more questions! \n======================================================================\n\nPLEASE DO NOT REPLY DIRECTLY TO THIS EMAIL!\nYou can reply to this personal conversation by following the link below:\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/index.php?app=members&module=messaging&section=view&do=findMessage&topicID=11488&msgID=__firstUnread__\n","Sender":{"Id":265511,"Name":"TinkerSofi","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-265511.jpg?_r=1442890536","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1442691312,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Conversation","RelatedItemId":11488},{"Id":116740,"Title":"mentioned you in this post","Message":"Hello!\n\nThis message is to notify you that ashhtayy mentioned you in a post.\n\nThe post that you were mentioned in can be found here:\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79584-azul-fives-20162017\/?view=findpost&p=1904716\n\n----------------------------------\n@\"hirvine83\" I'm getting married at AF June 7th, 2016. Selecting the resort was definitely the hardest part...until I laid my eyes on the Sky Deck and then I was sold. Although I too haven't done much planning we are booked for a 4:30 ceremony followed by a cocktail hour at the sky bar and reception on the Sky Deck. \n\nJust an FYI if you do go with AF - there is a fee for the Sky Deck. We booked and got it for $1700 but I believe it's gone up to $1800. In my mind it's well worth it for that fantastic view <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/>\n\nHappy Planning!\n----------------------------------\n\nIf you no longer wish to receive notifications of posts you are mentioned in, you can adjust your preferences on the\ncommunity by clicking My Settings, and then choosing Notification Options.\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/index.php\n\n","Sender":{"Id":282006,"Name":"ashhtayy","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-282006.png?_r=1423373502","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":138,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1442271101,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":116628,"Title":"liked a post you made in Azul Fives 2016\/2017","Message":"Hello!\n\nmotherofbridejanuary2016 just liked a post you made!\n======================================================================\nHi Everyone! My fiance and I are in the very beginning stages of planning our wedding in the Mayan Riviera for either November 2016 (likely) or Jan\/Feb 2017 (less likely). We are still trying to narrow down properties but I have so far absolutely fallen in love with Azul Fives, especially the...\n======================================================================\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/79584-azul-fives-20162017\/?view=findpost&p=1904576\n","Sender":{"Id":284812,"Name":"motherofbridejanuary2016","Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1442245974,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Post","RelatedItemId":0},{"Id":116513,"Title":"has replied to a personal conversation","Message":"hirvine83,\n\nreynbow has replied to a personal conversation entitled \"Congratulations\".\n\nreynbow said:\n======================================================================\nOops, I meant Melissa Mercado, not Michelle: http:\/\/melissa-mercado.com\/\n======================================================================\n\nPLEASE DO NOT REPLY DIRECTLY TO THIS EMAIL!\nYou can reply to this personal conversation by following the link below:\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/index.php?app=members&module=messaging&section=view&do=findMessage&topicID=11427&msgID=__firstUnread__\n","Sender":{"Id":276575,"Name":"reynbow","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-276575.jpg?_r=1424562947","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1442228115,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Conversation","RelatedItemId":11427},{"Id":116510,"Title":"has replied to a personal conversation","Message":"hirvine83,\n\nreynbow has replied to a personal conversation entitled \"Congratulations\".\n\nreynbow said:\n======================================================================\nThanks for your email. And congrats on your engagement and upcoming wedding!\n \nNot sure if you have this website, but it's for weddings at Karisma properties and if you're planning your wedding with their coordinators, Lomas. This website shows you all the options for decorations, flowers, DJ, photographer, etc:\n \nhttp:\/\/www.weddingsbylomastravel.com\/planning\/\n \nWe went to the Brides Dress Rehearsal and got to meet Lomas' photographers and view their work. But we ended up picking an outside photographer in part because we needed 4 days of shooting and Lomas' pricing didn't work for us.  We liked Sarani's work, but didn't care much for the work of the other photographers.  If you haven't heard about the Brides Dress Rehearsal, I'd be happy to share info. I highly recommend going to one if you're able to.\n \nIn case you don't know, Karisma charges $800 per outside vendor. However, if your vendor is a \"guest\" that stays 3 nights at the resort, then they waive the vendor fee. We paid for a room that was split between our outside DJ and photographer, so it ended up being about $600\/vendor instead of $800. But I heard that Azul Fives doesn't allow outside DJs anymore.\n \nAs for our photography package cost, since we paid for 4 days of shooting, this info probably won't be helpful for you. But our photographer, Pixan, does offer competitive pricing. If you're interested in hiring an outside DJ, I'd recommend Pixan and two other photographers, Naal Photography and Michelle Mercado.\n \nHope this info is helpful. Feel free to contact me with any additional questions. And good luck planning!\n \n-Reyna\n \n======================================================================\n\nPLEASE DO NOT REPLY DIRECTLY TO THIS EMAIL!\nYou can reply to this personal conversation by following the link below:\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/index.php?app=members&module=messaging&section=view&do=findMessage&topicID=11427&msgID=__firstUnread__\n","Sender":{"Id":276575,"Name":"reynbow","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-276575.jpg?_r=1424562947","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1442227643,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Conversation","RelatedItemId":11427},{"Id":116224,"Title":"started a new personal conversation with you","Message":"hirvine83,\n\nTammyWright has sent you a new personal conversation entitled \"Welcome hirvine83 to Best Destination Wedding\".\n\nTammyWright said:\n======================================================================\nHello hirvine83,<br \/><br \/>Welcome to BestDestinationWedding.com (BDW). BDW is the Ultimate Resource for planning your destination wedding. We have over 70,000 registered bride, grooms and vendors.<br \/><br \/>Here are some links and tips that might make your time here on BDW more enjoyable.<br \/><br \/>If you have not done so, you may want to:<br \/>complete your profile (upload a photo, add profile details, etc.)<br \/>visit the Newbies forum and introduce yourself (http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/f\/23\/newbies)<br \/>Start your own wedding planning blog (http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/blogs\/)<br \/>find the forum for your wedding destination and create a subscription to threads\/members\/vendors that you are interested in<br \/><br \/>Here are some links that may be helpful to you:<br \/>Destination Wedding Community & Forum (http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/f\/)<br \/>Resort Reviews (http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/products\/category\/resorts-villas)<br \/>Wedding Vendor Reviews (http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/products\/category\/wedding-vendors)<br \/>Destination Wedding Tips and Articles (http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/wedding-tips)<br \/>Wedding Image Gallery (http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/recent\/albums)<br \/>BDW Help Page (http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/index.php?app=core&module=help)<br \/>BDW Forum Rules and Etiquette (http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/8853\/forum-faqs-etiquette-rules)<br \/>How to Download Attachments (http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/48545\/update-1-18-2010-downloading-attachments)<br \/><br \/>Here are some BDW members and staff you should follow:<br \/><br \/>Moderators and Community Leaders<br \/>Tammy Host - Founder and Owner of BDW (http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/206696-tammy-host\/). Tammy got married at Dreams Los Cabos in 2006<br \/>AlexisinJamaica (http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/255437-alexisinjamaica\/) - Moderator & Community Leader. Alexis got married in Jamaica in 2013.<br \/><br \/>If you would like to \"like\" or \"follow\" us, here are our BDW accounts:<br \/>BDW on Facebook (http:\/\/www.facebook.com\/BDWForum)<br \/>BDW on Twitter (http:\/\/twitter.com\/BDWForum)<br \/>BDW on Pinterest (http:\/\/pinterest.com\/bdwforum\/)<br \/><br \/>If you are a vendor and looking to advertise your business, please email advertise@bestdestinationwedding.com (mailto:advertise@bestdestinationwedding.com?subject=Advertising%20Inquiry%20for%20BDW).<br \/><br \/>Vendor rules are HERE! Please read! (http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/t\/921\/vendor-business-membership-fees-rules-updated-6-18-2010)<br \/><br \/>Please feel free to browse around and get to know others. If you have any questions please don't hesitate to ask. Hope you enjoy your time here.<br \/><br \/>Team BDW\n======================================================================\n\nPLEASE DO NOT REPLY DIRECTLY TO THIS EMAIL!\nYou can reply to this personal conversation by following the link below:\n\nhttp:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/index.php?app=members&module=messaging&section=view&do=showConversation&topicID=11421#msg20410\n","Sender":{"Id":206696,"Name":"TammyWright","Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-206696.jpg?_r=1386394555","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":135,"PhotoType":"custom"},"IsOnline":false},"NotificationDate":1442062591,"IsRead":true,"RelatedItemType":"Conversation","RelatedItemId":11421}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":"8","TotalPages":1,"CurrentPage":0,"NextPage":-1,"PreviousPage":-1,"LastPage":0},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}